Z||000015||turbo86se||08-18-2001||01:15 PM||||You'll love your new job. Congrats and good luck. <P>Back in '93, I was a lot attendant at the Saturn dealership. I had a lot of freedom, they let me do whatever I wanted, as long as the sold and showroom cars were spotless, lot cars were reasonably clean and had gas. I used to love that job. I could clean my own car whenever I wanted. I would set a goal for the day, I'd pick out a car, usually a SC2 or SL2 clean it up real nice and set it up under the canopy. I'd get little rewards if that car was sold that day. <P>I also loved the Dealer Exchanges. I'd get to take a Saturn home for the night, and take a road trip the next day. One time I went about 6 hours away and kept the cars for two days.<P>In winter, when parts of the lot froze, I'd drive down 20 mph or so, slam on the brakes and slide all over the place! Of course that doesn't work with the ABS brakes!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Then there was the time when I was at my boss' Christmas party. Got a little drunk, stayed the night, and hooked up with his daughter. That was the last X-mas party I was invited to! LOL<P>Let us know how it turns out!! ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Galen||08-18-2001||08:43 PM||||funny perhaps, but the only place I flip burgers is my own kitchen. I dont work, I dont need to work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A>||||reg||1
